    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve the equation \\((x - 5)^2 = 9\\) and find the sum of its roots, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Solve the equation for \\(x\\):**\n\n   The given equation is:\n   \\[\n   (x - 5)^2 = 9\n   \\]\n\n   To eliminate the square, we take the square root of both sides:\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{(x - 5)^2} = \\sqrt{9}\n   \\]\n\n   This simplifies to:\n   \\[\n   x - 5 = \\pm 3\n   \\]\n\n   Therefore, we have two separate equations to solve:\n   \\[\n   x - 5 = 3 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad x - 5 = -3\n   \\]\n\n2. **Solve each equation:**\n\n   For the first equation:\n   \\[\n   x - 5 = 3\n   \\]\n   Add 5 to both sides:\n   \\[\n   x = 3 + 5\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   x = 8\n   \\]\n\n   For the second equation:\n   \\[\n   x - 5 = -3\n   \\]\n   Add 5 to both sides:\n   \\[\n   x = -3 + 5\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   x = 2\n   \\]\n\n   So, the solutions to the equation \\((x - 5)^2 = 9\\) are \\(x = 8\\) and \\(x = 2\\).\n\n3. **Find the sum of the roots:**\n\n   The roots of the equation are \\(x = 8\\) and \\(x = 2\\). To find the sum of these roots, we add them together:\n   \\[\n   8 + 2 = 10\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the roots of the equation \\((x - 5)^2 = 9\\) is \\(\\boxed{10}\\).",
